# Copy to .env.docker (git-ignored) and fill in real host paths before running
# `docker compose --env-file .env.docker up -d`. The --env-file flag is
# required in addition to the `env_file:` entry in docker-compose.yml: Compose
# only reads variables for its own ${...} substitution (the port-publish line)
# from the file passed via --env-file, while `env_file:` controls what is
# injected into the container's own process environment. Passing both keeps
# HOMEBASE_PORT consistent between the published port and the app itself.

# Required: absolute host path to the directory containing sibling
# application repositories. Bind-mounted read-only at /workspace.
HOMEBASE_HOST_WORKSPACE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/projects

# Required: absolute host path to an existing, writable directory for
# HomeBase's own log file and one writable subdirectory per configured
# application. Bind-mounted read-write at /data. Must already exist and be
# writable by UID 1000 (the runtime image's non-root "node" user) before the
# first run.
HOMEBASE_HOST_DATA_PATH=/absolute/path/to/data

# Required: absolute host path to the operational, git-ignored registry file.
# Bind-mounted read-only at /app/config/homebase.json.
HOMEBASE_HOST_CONFIG_PATH=/absolute/path/to/homebase.json

# Required only if the DevPlanner application is enabled in the mounted
# registry: absolute host path to DevPlanner's own workspace directory
# (boards/cards data and its own backups, distinct from HOMEBASE_DATA_PATH).
# Bind-mounted read-write at /mnt/devplanner-workspace; the registry's
# devplanner adapterConfig.workspacePath must be set to that container path.
# If DevPlanner is disabled, point this at any existing empty directory.
HOMEBASE_HOST_DEVPLANNER_WORKSPACE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/devplanner-workspace

# Required only if DevPlanner's registry entry sets adapterConfig.
# fileBrowserBasePath/artifactBasePath: absolute host path to the vault root
# those two settings resolve within. Bind-mounted read-write at
# /mnt/devplanner-vault; the registry's fileBrowserBasePath must be set to
# that container path (and artifactBasePath to a subdirectory of it, e.g.
# /mnt/devplanner-vault/10-Projects). If unused, point this at any existing
# empty directory.
HOMEBASE_HOST_DEVPLANNER_VAULT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/devplanner-vault

# Required: absolute host path to a git-credential-store file granting HTTPS auth
# for private repositories git needs to read from inside the container (e.g. the
# AgentVault vault above, if its remote is private). Bind-mounted read-only at
# /run/secrets/git-credentials. Format: one line,
# https://x-access-token:<PAT>@github.com — see git-credentials.docker.example.
# Use a GitHub fine-grained PAT scoped to read-only Contents access on only the
# specific repositories needed; never a classic or broad-scope token, and never
# put the token directly in this .env.docker file as a plain variable (env vars
# are visible via `docker inspect`; a mounted file is not). If no private repos
# are in use, point this at any existing empty file. See README.md's "Git
# credentials for private repositories" section for full setup steps.
HOMEBASE_HOST_GIT_CREDENTIALS_PATH=/absolute/path/to/git-credentials.docker

# Optional: overrides server.port from the mounted registry, and is also used
# to compute the host-loopback published port. Defaults to 17106 if unset.
# HOMEBASE_PORT=17106

# Optional: informational public origin surfaced to hosted adapters.
# HOMEBASE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://home.example.ts.net

# Optional: minimum level written to the NDJSON log. One of
# trace|debug|info|warn|error|fatal. Defaults to info.
# HOMEBASE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Optional (dev stack only): comma-separated hostnames the containerized Vite
# dev server accepts requests for beyond localhost, e.g. a Tailscale
# MagicDNS name. Consumed by vite.config.ts via loadEnv; this file's
# env_file mount is how it reaches the homebase-dev container's environment
# (the repo-root .env used by local `npm run dev` is not read by Compose).
# VITE_DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=home.example.ts.net
